+# Purpose: tool-powershell
+
+Maintenance context; never loaded at inference.
+
+Answers a mined lesson (4 sessions, 3 repos) where the PowerShell tool failed
+repeatedly: runs ending in a bare `Exit code 1` six and eight times in a row,
+and a `Remove-Item` on a protected system path that was refused and then
+retried. Triage: not mechanical, because the failures only show at run time and
+no commit, push or CI input exposes them (see the record's triage reason).
+
+Decisions taken without a person to ask (skill-creator non-interactive flow):
+the skill is machine-bound (adam-coding-local) because it concerns Windows
+interop; it points to `windows-elevation-from-wsl` for the elevation case
+instead of repeating it; it says to stop at a protected path and hand over,
+not to look for a workaround.
